---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CtaStrip from '../components/CtaStrip.astro';
import QuickAnswer from '../components/QuickAnswer.astro';
import RelatedLinks from '../components/RelatedLinks.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
import { breadcrumbSchema, localBusinessSchema, coreServiceSchema } from '../lib/schema';

const schema = [
  localBusinessSchema(),
  coreServiceSchema(),
  breadcrumbSchema([
    { name: 'Home', url: SITE.url },
    { name: 'Why ABS', url: `${SITE.url}/why-abs/` },
  ]),
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Anti-Snap Lock Fitting: Why We Fit Avocet ABS"
  description="Why kianlocks fits one euro cylinder — Avocet ABS, TS007 3-star and Sold Secure Diamond — what the ratings mean, and what you get for £149 in London."
  schema={schema}
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Why ABS' }]} />
      <h1>The case for fitting one cylinder, properly.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Most lock changes go wrong before the locksmith arrives — at the
        point of brand selection. Here&rsquo;s why we made a deliberate choice
        to carry one cylinder and only one.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <article class="prose">
        <QuickAnswer>
          <p>
            We fit Avocet ABS because it holds the two top UK cylinder grades — BSI Kitemark
            TS007 3-star and Sold Secure SS312 Diamond — plus Secured by Design (Police Preferred
            Specification) accreditation, in a range that fits almost any euro-profile door.
            Other brands reach the same grades; standardising on one tested product means
            every door we fit gets the same protection, keys and guarantee.
          </p>
        </QuickAnswer>

        <h2>The euro cylinder is the door</h2>
        <p>
          On the vast majority of London front doors — uPVC, composite,
          and most timber — the entire security of the door rests on the
          euro-profile cylinder. The handle is cosmetic. The multipoint
          mechanism is robust but only as strong as the cylinder it
          accepts. If the cylinder fails, the door is open.
        </p>
        <p>
          Cylinders fail in four ways under attack: snapping, bumping,
          picking and drilling. A &lsquo;snap attack&rsquo; — where the
          cylinder is gripped with mole grips and twisted until it shears
          — needs no specialist tools and, on a vulnerable cylinder, can take
          seconds. Police forces and the Master Locksmiths Association have
          warned about it for over a decade. Read more in
          <a href="/guides/lock-snapping-explained/">lock snapping explained</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What 3-star actually means</h2>
        <p>
          The British Standard for euro cylinders is TS007. It awards
          stars: 1, 2 or 3. To get 3 stars, a cylinder must independently
          defeat all four attack methods in standardised testing. To get
          1 star, it only has to defeat some of them — and in real-world
          installations, a 1-star cylinder is meant to be paired with a
          2-star handle to make up the rating.
        </p>
        <p>
          That works on paper. In practice, handles get changed. Doors
          get refurbished. The 2-star handle is replaced by something
          off Amazon and the door silently drops back to 1-star without
          anyone noticing.
        </p>
        <p>
          A 3-star cylinder doesn&rsquo;t have that problem. It is
          independently rated. The handle can be anything. The cylinder
          alone meets the standard.
        </p>

        <h2>Why Avocet ABS specifically</h2>
        <p>
          There are several 3-star cylinders on the UK market — we compare
          them honestly in <a href="/guides/best-anti-snap-euro-cylinders-uk/">anti-snap
          cylinders compared</a>. We chose Avocet ABS because:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>It holds Sold Secure SS312 Diamond as well as TS007 3-star. Diamond is the highest grade Sold Secure awards a cylinder.</li>
          <li>It carries Secured by Design (Police Preferred Specification) accreditation.</li>
          <li>Avocet lists the current ABS Master against the updated TS007-1:2024 standard, which adds freezing and gluing attacks to the tests.</li>
          <li>Avocet describes a cam that locks down inside a hardened core when the cylinder is snapped, so the lock stays locked even after an attack.</li>
          <li>The range covers standard euro doubles and thumbturn versions in a wide spread of lengths, so we can size to the door rather than make do.</li>
          <li>Keys come with a registration card, so copies can be controlled.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Why we don&rsquo;t carry alternatives</h2>
        <p>
          If we stocked five brands of cylinder, we would fit five
          brands of cylinder — and the cheapest ones, when the customer
          chose price over rating, would underperform. The honest
          version of this trade is to carry the best product and quote
          its real cost. That&rsquo;s what we do.
        </p>
        <p>
          We are not the cheapest locksmith in London. We are not trying
          to be. We are trying to be the locksmith you call when you
          want the cylinder problem solved once and never thought about
          again.
        </p>

        <h2>What you get</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>An Avocet ABS cylinder, sized to your door and fitted in one visit.</li>
          <li>Three keys for your new cylinder.</li>
          <li>An itemised written invoice naming the product and its ratings — for your insurer, landlord or freeholder.</li>
          <li>Avocet&rsquo;s own manufacturer guarantee, on Avocet&rsquo;s terms.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="meta-line">Product facts checked against Avocet and Sold Secure listings on {SITE.factsReviewed.split('-').reverse().join('/')}.</p>

        <RelatedLinks links={[
          { href: '/guides/ts007-3-star-explained/', title: 'TS007 3-star explained', blurb: 'What the stars mean and how to check your door.' },
          { href: '/guides/best-anti-snap-euro-cylinders-uk/', title: 'Anti-snap cylinders compared', blurb: 'ABS, Ultion, Yale, Mul-T-Lock and more.' },
          { href: '/3-star-lock-upgrade-london/', title: 'Upgrade to a 3-star lock', blurb: `${SITE.price} flat, fitted across North & Central London and Hertfordshire.` },
        ]} />
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaStrip
    heading={`Ready to upgrade? ${SITE.price} flat.`}
    body="One cylinder, one visit, one fixed price. Email us with your postcode and door type — we'll come back within 2 hours with a slot."
  />
</BaseLayout>
